  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved governance of labour migration and mobility in line with ILS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This programme supports Barbados in strengthening labour migration governance to ensure that labour mobility contributes to decent work, inclusive growth, and sustainable economic transformation. As Barbados implements full free movement arrangements within the Caribbean Community Secretariat (CARICOM) and responds to demographic change, skills shortages, and economic diversification priorities, a coherent and rights-based labour migration framework has become essential. 

Aligned with the Barbados Decent Work Country Programme (DWCP) 2025&#x2013;2030 and ILO Programme and Budget Outcome 6: Protection at work for all, the initiative provides technical assistance to develop and adopt a comprehensive national labour migration policy and action plan, strengthen labour migration data systems, and update the national migrant labour protocol. Through enhanced tripartite dialogue, improved labour market information, and strengthened protection mechanisms, the programme aims to safeguard migrant workers&#x2019; rights, promote fair and orderly labour mobility, and ensure that migration supports workforce sustainability, enterprise development, and climate-resilient growth in Barbados.</narrative>
  </description>
